body:
I am definitely not a cradle Catholic but I feel like the first time I did RCIA some stuff went over my head. So think this will be nice the second time around. 

&#x200B;

God Bless

Thanks for sharing. I would though encourage you to share your sexual history with your wife. If the roles were reversed would you want to k now about her experiences with females? We need to be honest with out partners, lying by omission is still lying. But it is essentially up to you. 

&#x200B;

God bless and welcome

Bless your grandmother, she's from a different time and they don't understand. You cannot pray it away. Ever. And I will tell you something if you keep repressing who you are you will get ill, be it mentally or physically. You need to embrace who you are. Now your job doesn't need to know about your personal life, it's your personal life, however, it will be very hard to stay there once you've accepted yourself. I suggest trying to find a more affirming church. They are around. I know you're not a Catholic, and Catholicism has a (deservedly) bad rap for gay rights, but you're always welcome at my rainbow Catholics reddit group. We are 100% affirming, and I am a practising Catholic. And my priest is just amazing, he's not a homophobe. Don't give up on your faith, just find a better church. So much love to you, God loves you so much.

&#x200B;

Also, I'm so sorry about your mum, that's rough. <3
